<header><p class="st-kicker">republic · South Asia</p><h1 class="st-title">Federal Democratic Republic of Nepal</h1><p class="st-meta">2008 CE – present · capital Kathmandu</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Nepal's federal republic, created when the Constituent Assembly abolished the Shah monarchy in 2008.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>After the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/2006-peoples-movement">2006 People's Movement</a> ended <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gyanendra-of-nepal">King Gyanendra</a>'s direct rule and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nepalese-civil-war">Maoist insurgency</a>, a peace agreement brought the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/communist-party-of-nepal-maoist-centre">Maoists</a> into politics. The elected Constituent Assembly declared <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-nepal">Nepal</a> a federal democratic republic on 28 May 2008, abolishing the Kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nepal">Nepal</a>, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ram-baran-yadav">Ram Baran Yadav</a> became the first president.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Governments have changed frequently, led by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nepali-congress">Nepali Congress</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/communist-party-of-nepal-unified-marxist-leninist">Communist Party of Nepal (UML)</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/communist-party-of-nepal-maoist-centre">Maoist Centre</a>; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pushpa-kamal-dahal">Pushpa Kamal Dahal</a> (Prachanda) served several terms as prime minister. A devastating earthquake struck in 2015, and the same year a new constitution created seven federal provinces and a secular state. Remittances from workers abroad and tourism support the economy.</p><h2>To the present</h2><p>The republic continues. Youth-led protests in September 2025 forced the resignation of prime minister <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/k-p-sharma-oli">K. P. Sharma Oli</a>, and an interim government under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sushila-karki">Sushila Karki</a> was formed and called elections for March 2026.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/federal-democratic-republic-of-nepal.jpg" alt="Federal Democratic Republic of Nepal" width="320" height="271"><figcaption>Image: Biplab Anand · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Emblem_of_Nepal.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>2008 CE – present</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/21st-century">21st century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>republic</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Kathmandu</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Ram Baran Yadav, Pushpa Kamal Dahal, K. P. Sharma Oli</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Hinduism, Buddhism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Nepali</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/nepal">Nepal</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Nepal (republic), Republic of Nepal</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=2017&amp;focus=federal-democratic-republic-of-nepal" aria-label="Federal Democratic Republic of Nepal on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="6919 1162 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Federal Democratic Republic of Nepal lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M7239 1418L7239 1418"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M7239 1418h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M7239 1418h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M7239 1418h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Kathmandu. <a href="/atlas?year=2017&amp;focus=federal-democratic-republic-of-nepal">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
